Three results emerged.

- Proved a chemical-potential range bound of \(8M\) for integer-normalized charges, hence an integrated curvature bound including Mott cusp contributions.
- Assuming local real-time Luttinger matching, proved \(v_a\le6\mathrm e M\) using Lieb–Robinson locality. Thus \(D e''\le36\mathrm e^2M^2\) for a non-drifting single sector, so large curvature forces small stiffness.
- If microscopic charges independently resolve every Gaussian mode, this gives \(A_{\mathrm{U(1)}}\le6\mathrm e M(d-1)\).

The general sum remains open. Several modes can couple to the same charge, so nonzero coupling does not justify the proposed sector count. A pointwise bound on smooth \(e''\) alone also remains unproved.

